  "notes": "Near-black HUD/cockpit look: floating 18px-radius black panels with thin borders and shadows over a tilted dark 3D map of Macau. Warm amber (#fcd34d) marks active state (pause button, selected speed 1×, active road-works card with amber border and fill, histogram bars). Mint green dots mean live. Every label is bilingual: a tracked uppercase English mono eyebrow over a Chinese title (e.g. PARISHES / 堂區). Numbered sections (01 城市日常, 02 城市專題) and tab indices (01/02) give it an atlas/instrument feel. The clock uses a split HH:MM in large mono with a yellow colon and the seconds in a side column. The timeline doubles as a histogram of transit service density, with 早尖峰/晚尖峰 peak callouts and first/last service markers (首班 06:30, 末班 23:15). The hidden left menu holds 2D/3D/buildings/dark mode/timeline toggles, a font-size control, a ZH/PT/EN language switch and a list of data sources (not visible in the capture). The live page could not be opened."
